00:16:05.536 --> 00:16:08.596
BRITT: That's it.
BREE: Ow! Mom!


00:16:10.608 --> 00:16:12.269
Have another crab puff, Rod.


00:16:13.044 --> 00:16:16.138
Mom, he's hungry. It's been 40 minutes.


00:16:16.781 --> 00:16:19.409
Look, you asked me to come, I'm here.


00:16:19.584 --> 00:16:23.020
- But five more minutes and I'm out.
- I'm right behind you, JP.


00:16:25.690 --> 00:16:29.148
Joey, I know that you and Dominique
have had your differences...


00:16:29.327 --> 00:16:32.763
...but try not to bring up
the time she dissed you on <i>TRL.</i>


00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:33.954
She didn't mean it.


00:16:34.132 --> 00:16:36.999
How do you call someone overrated
and not mean it? That's just disrespect.


00:16:37.168 --> 00:16:38.260
Shh.


00:16:40.004 --> 00:16:44.407
Joey, doing a duet with Dominique
means reaching her audience.


00:16:44.575 --> 00:16:46.008
Like Daddy and I.


00:16:46.477 --> 00:16:48.411
And if doing a duet means that Mommy...


00:16:50.214 --> 00:16:54.344
- The family can have another house, well...
- Okay, Mom, you have a house.


00:16:54.619 --> 00:16:55.643
Okay?


00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:58.789
Nobody's bought a Dominique CD
in years. I mean, she's not cool.


00:16:58.956 --> 00:16:59.980
I think she's cool.


00:17:01.059 --> 00:17:02.959
Thank you. Exactly.


00:17:03.127 --> 00:17:04.617
DOMINIQUE:
Hi.


00:17:05.530 --> 00:17:10.126
Look at all of these beautiful people.


00:17:10.301 --> 00:17:12.428
Well, I'm so sorry
to keep you all waiting.


00:17:12.603 --> 00:17:16.004
But it took 20 minutes
to descend the staircase.


00:17:16.174 --> 00:17:18.642
But it was worth it, don't you think?


00:17:18.976 --> 00:17:20.500
Hello, Rod. No, no.


00:17:20.678 --> 00:17:22.976
Evie. No, no, no.


00:17:23.147 --> 00:17:25.342
- Young man whose name I don't know.
- I'm...


00:17:25.516 --> 00:17:26.710
Oh. Shh.


00:17:26.884 --> 00:17:28.852
ROD:
Wow, that's some dress.


00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:32.114
Oh, yeah?
I'm wearing this in my next video.


00:17:32.290 --> 00:17:35.225
It's a duet, great stuff.


00:17:35.393 --> 00:17:37.486
Hello, Grammy. Ha-ha-ha.


00:17:37.662 --> 00:17:38.686
[LAUGHING]


00:17:38.863 --> 00:17:41.195
But enough about me, for now.


00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:43.795
ROD:
Oh, let me help you.


00:17:43.968 --> 00:17:45.196
- Yeah. Um...
DOMINIQUE: Thank you.


00:17:45.369 --> 00:17:47.234
Look, Dominique...


00:17:48.406 --> 00:17:51.307
...I'm not doing the duet with you, okay?


00:17:51.476 --> 00:17:53.137
No, listen to what she has to say.


00:17:53.311 --> 00:17:54.642
DOMINIQUE: Zip it, Rod.
ROD: Or not.


00:17:54.812 --> 00:17:56.837
Drinks, we need drinks. Mary?


00:17:57.381 --> 00:17:59.144
Well, thanks, but I don't drink.


00:17:59.317 --> 00:18:01.979
- Oh, my God.
JOEY: Sorry. Thank you.


00:18:02.353 --> 00:18:04.719
Of course you don't, darling boy,
but I do.


00:18:04.889 --> 00:18:06.686
- Okay.
- I drink.


00:18:06.958 --> 00:18:08.255
- So, Joey...
- I'll get you one.


00:18:08.426 --> 00:18:10.485
...asked anyone
to the Black and White Ball yet?


00:18:10.661 --> 00:18:12.856
You have a crab puff in your teeth, Britt.


00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:15.191
- You should really take me to the ball.
- Yeah.


00:18:15.366 --> 00:18:18.199
I speak French. How about you?


00:18:18.369 --> 00:18:19.631
Thanks, yeah.


00:18:19.804 --> 00:18:23.296
Look, Dominique, I'm kind of on a break
right now, so...


00:18:23.474 --> 00:18:26.932
You all must be famished.
First course, Mary. Now.


00:18:27.678 --> 00:18:31.114
Joey would gladly take a break
from his break.


00:18:31.282 --> 00:18:34.080
No. No, no.
Actually, I am focusing on school.


00:18:34.252 --> 00:18:38.211
- I'm just hanging with friends, you know?
- That's right. The new JP.


00:18:38.389 --> 00:18:39.617
Who are you?


00:18:39.791 --> 00:18:41.258
I'm Joey Parker's manager.


00:18:41.425 --> 00:18:44.121
Oh, please ignore him.


00:18:44.295 --> 00:18:45.922
I'm Joey's manager.


00:18:46.097 --> 00:18:47.758
BRITT:
You have two managers?


00:18:47.932 --> 00:18:50.594
- Apparently.
- You must be a real handful.


00:18:50.768 --> 00:18:52.201
Wanna make out?


00:18:52.370 --> 00:18:54.235
You know, actually, technically, I'm...


00:18:54.405 --> 00:18:57.704
Oh, shut up, Rod. Even I know
you're completely inconsequential.


00:18:57.875 --> 00:18:59.433
You see? It's not just me.


00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:01.771
JOEY:
This is why I did not wanna come today.


00:19:02.647 --> 00:19:03.875
You're all nuts.


00:19:04.282 --> 00:19:08.150
You can either do the duet with me
and become a superstar...


00:19:08.319 --> 00:19:13.052
...or you can fade away
into teenybopper obscurity.


00:19:13.224 --> 00:19:15.954
Okay. I've heard enough, okay?


00:19:16.127 --> 00:19:18.595
Joey Parker is a man
that needs to do things his way.


00:19:18.763 --> 00:19:23.826
He needs to keep it real. So from here
on out, I'm Joey Parker's only manager.


00:19:24.001 --> 00:19:25.525
I think we're done here. Let's go.


00:19:25.703 --> 00:19:27.000
Thanks for everything.


00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:32.632
We keep meeting like this.


00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:35.438
You have shrimp in your hair.


00:19:35.613 --> 00:19:36.739
DUSTIN:
Come on.


00:19:36.914 --> 00:19:38.245
- You all right?
EVIE: That's nuts.


00:19:38.416 --> 00:19:40.281
- You hear how he...?
ROD: I don't care!


00:19:40.451 --> 00:19:42.078
DUSTIN: Are you ready?
- Mary?


00:19:42.253 --> 00:19:43.277
DUSTIN:
Let's go.


00:19:43.454 --> 00:19:48.323
You will clean this room spotless
in 30 minutes. Rod.


00:19:49.961 --> 00:19:53.419
And your phone privileges are suspended
for an entire month. Cough it up.


00:19:53.598 --> 00:19:54.963
Come on, look alive.


00:19:55.499 --> 00:19:57.467
Clean.


00:19:57.635 --> 00:19:59.364
Joey, honey, wait.


00:19:59.537 --> 00:20:01.596
I gotta talk to you.


00:20:07.278 --> 00:20:08.939
Tami, don't hate me...


00:20:10.948 --> 00:20:12.939
...but I don't wanna go to the ball.


00:20:13.117 --> 00:20:16.052
You have to go. I've been working
on our dresses for two weeks.


00:20:16.220 --> 00:20:18.415
I know. I know. It's just...


00:20:18.589 --> 00:20:22.116
I don't know. It's on Valentine's Day.
We don't even have dates.


00:20:22.293 --> 00:20:25.194
Plus, everyone's gonna be wearing masks,
which is really weird.


00:20:25.363 --> 00:20:29.129
But that's good. We can each meet
a handsome, mysterious stranger.


00:20:29.400 --> 00:20:31.868
How will we know he's handsome
if he's wearing a mask?


00:20:32.036 --> 00:20:34.561
By how he dances.
Hot guys always dance the best.


00:20:34.739 --> 00:20:36.263
- Anyway...
- I don't fit in here.


00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:38.806
So why go and pretend like I do?


00:20:38.976 --> 00:20:40.409
Guys don't even know I exist.


00:20:40.578 --> 00:20:43.138
Again, no one will know who anyone is.


00:20:43.314 --> 00:20:45.680
There's no such thing as not fitting in.


00:20:45.850 --> 00:20:48.182
If there's a guy you like,
he'll meet the real you.


00:20:48.352 --> 00:20:52.152
Not some fake you that's been created
by the cliques at our lame-ass high school.


00:20:52.323 --> 00:20:54.314
- Don't get me started about... What?
- Tami.


00:20:54.492 --> 00:20:57.120
You should really breathe
in between monologues.


00:20:57.295 --> 00:20:58.922
You're going to the ball.


00:21:00.231 --> 00:21:01.926
Oh, I forgot to start cleaning.


00:21:02.767 --> 00:21:04.632
DOMINIQUE:
<i>Faster.</i>


00:21:06.137 --> 00:21:08.332
Give it a rhythm. Make it a samba.


00:21:08.506 --> 00:21:09.666
Give it a:


00:21:09.840 --> 00:21:11.364
[HUMMING]


00:21:13.477 --> 00:21:14.774
- Mother.
- Mommy?


00:21:14.946 --> 00:21:16.413
Hello, my little pretties.


00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:20.641
This is Fabio and Paulo
and somebody else.


00:21:20.818 --> 00:21:23.912
I'm thinking of making one of them
my new daddy.


00:21:24.488 --> 00:21:26.422
I mean, your new daddy.


00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:28.581
Anyway, uh...


00:21:28.759 --> 00:21:31.819
...we were on our way to get manis
and pedis for the ball tonight.


00:21:31.996 --> 00:21:35.432
Which we heard Mary talking about, FYI.


00:21:35.599 --> 00:21:38.295
As in she's planning to go, FYI.


00:21:39.070 --> 00:21:40.401
Oh. Oh...


00:21:40.571 --> 00:21:42.436
That won't do.


00:21:43.374 --> 00:21:45.706
Uh, you could tell her to clean my room.


00:21:45.876 --> 00:21:48.037
And my closet.
I think something died in there.


00:21:48.212 --> 00:21:50.009
No, no, no.


00:21:50.181 --> 00:21:55.949
I have a very special place
that needs cleaning.


00:21:57.788 --> 00:21:58.948
DOMINIQUE:
Mary?


00:22:00.524 --> 00:22:04.221
- The twins are turning 16 next week.
- Didn't they turn 16 last year?


00:22:04.595 --> 00:22:08.361
Yes, and they'll keep turning 16
until I tell them to stop.


00:22:08.532 --> 00:22:12.525
We're having a big party
and I need this house to be spotless.


00:22:12.703 --> 00:22:16.969
But Tami and I are going to the ball.
Plus, I've cleaned every room in this house.


00:22:17.141 --> 00:22:18.733
Not...


00:22:20.244 --> 00:22:22.007
...my bedroom.


00:22:27.151 --> 00:22:29.517
You're kidding me, right?


00:22:30.354 --> 00:22:31.821
I'm clubbing with Paris tonight.


00:22:31.989 --> 00:22:35.652
It's my turn to throw the after-party.
Don't step on my hair.


00:22:35.826 --> 00:22:40.695
When I get home at midnight,
this room will be pristine.


00:22:40.865 --> 00:22:44.198
Dominique, I'd need heavy equipment.
For example, a flamethrower.


00:22:44.568 --> 00:22:47.867
Don't you sass me, smarty pants.


00:22:48.039 --> 00:22:50.098
I'll revoke your school privileges.


00:22:50.274 --> 00:22:52.504
You could say goodbye
to those trendy friends.


00:22:52.676 --> 00:22:58.114
Or shall I say friend,
Little Miss Not-So-Popular?


00:22:58.282 --> 00:22:59.306
[CHUCKLES]


00:23:00.351 --> 00:23:01.375
Ooh!


00:23:02.086 --> 00:23:05.385
Oh, and clean up these fish sticks.
They've been there since Lent.


00:23:09.627 --> 00:23:10.992
[PHONE RINGS]


00:23:11.929 --> 00:23:13.362
MARY:
<i>Tami, I can't go to the ball.</i>


00:23:13.531 --> 00:23:15.465
"Domifreak's" making me clean
her bedroom.


00:23:16.000 --> 00:23:17.968
You're in her lair?


00:23:18.135 --> 00:23:21.229
There are species of bugs in here
still unknown to science.


00:23:21.405 --> 00:23:23.805
<i>There's no way I'll finish in time.</i>


00:23:24.275 --> 00:23:26.243
- Wait, what if...?
DOMINIQUE: <i>Who are you talking to?</i>


00:23:26.744 --> 00:23:30.077
<i>When I said no phone privileges,</i>
<i>that included the landline.</i>


00:23:30.247 --> 00:23:31.805
I'm sorry. I have to go.


00:23:40.658 --> 00:23:42.023
Ugh.


00:23:56.540 --> 00:23:57.871
[RUSTLING]


00:24:12.656 --> 00:24:13.987
[GROWLING]


00:24:17.194 --> 00:24:18.525
[BARKING]


00:24:18.696 --> 00:24:22.860
Manson, we've been looking for you
since Christmas, boy.


00:24:23.033 --> 00:24:25.024
You're free, boy. Go. Go, go.


00:24:27.872 --> 00:24:29.362
[DOORBELL RINGS]


00:24:32.276 --> 00:24:34.471
Go, Manson, go. You're free. Oh, hey.


00:24:34.645 --> 00:24:38.274
Gosh, look, I just found Manson.
And please tell me those aren't our dresses.


00:24:38.682 --> 00:24:41.310
I can't. Because they are.


00:24:41.485 --> 00:24:43.146
We're going to the ball.


00:24:43.320 --> 00:24:47.222
Tami, what part of "Domifreak's making me
clean her bedroom" did you not understand?


00:24:47.791 --> 00:24:51.192
What would you say if I told you
I could clean up the mess for you...


00:24:51.362 --> 00:24:53.455
...and Dominique would never know?


00:24:53.631 --> 00:24:57.397
I'd say you're my hero, but there's no way,
and you have to go to the ball.


00:24:57.568 --> 00:25:02.164
- Plus, you can't clean this mess up alone.
- Well, who said I was alone?


00:25:03.474 --> 00:25:04.498
- Hi, Mary.
- Hey.


00:25:05.142 --> 00:25:06.507
You did this for me?


00:25:06.677 --> 00:25:09.407
Mary, meet my sister's
boyfriend's cousins.


00:25:09.580 --> 00:25:12.048
Cousins, this is Mary.


00:25:12.216 --> 00:25:14.411
Hello, hello. You go to dance?


00:25:14.585 --> 00:25:15.847
Very nice.


00:25:16.020 --> 00:25:17.248
House clean by midnight?


00:25:17.421 --> 00:25:22.154
No problem. Like van say, "No mess...


00:25:22.326 --> 00:25:24.590
...too messy."
- Okay.


00:25:27.164 --> 00:25:28.722
This mess is too messy.


00:25:28.899 --> 00:25:31.424
- Lee-Ha, you promised.
- Is there a problem?


00:25:31.602 --> 00:25:34.537
I'm on it. Get started and hide the van.


00:25:36.574 --> 00:25:38.565
[MUSIC PLAYING]


00:25:38.742 --> 00:25:39.868
BREE:
Isn't that him?


00:25:40.044 --> 00:25:43.411
No, that's not him.
Oh, that's him. No, it's not.


00:25:44.548 --> 00:25:46.072
Joey can dance.


00:25:46.250 --> 00:25:48.684
When we see a guy who can move,
we'll have our man.


00:25:48.852 --> 00:25:50.945
Let me know when you find him.


00:25:51.121 --> 00:25:54.056
Hey, we were just looking for you.


00:25:54.225 --> 00:25:57.023
Yeah, I'm sure you were.


00:25:58.295 --> 00:26:00.627
- Nice mask.
- Nice dress.


00:26:00.798 --> 00:26:02.789
Nice face.


00:26:04.535 --> 00:26:06.298
Hey, ladies, hey.


00:26:06.470 --> 00:26:09.462
Boo, where you going?
All the funk you need is right here.


00:26:09.640 --> 00:26:10.971
[CHUCKLES]


00:26:12.576 --> 00:26:14.203
Man.


00:26:14.645 --> 00:26:15.907
Hey, man.


00:26:16.080 --> 00:26:18.275
Why did you tell me this
was a costume party?


00:26:18.449 --> 00:26:19.882
It is the Black and White Ball.


00:26:20.050 --> 00:26:21.642
You look good, man. This is sharp.


00:26:21.819 --> 00:26:23.844
I do clean up good, huh?


00:26:25.055 --> 00:26:27.489
I guess I'm not the only one
who didn't get the memo.


00:26:29.660 --> 00:26:32.493
- Who is that?
- No idea.


00:26:33.664 --> 00:26:35.097
But I'm gonna find out.


00:26:35.532 --> 00:26:36.931
Everyone's looking at me.


00:26:37.101 --> 00:26:40.002
Who's the Lohan
who decided to make her own rules?


00:26:40.170 --> 00:26:42.229
You need a drink.
Punch bowl, straight ahead.


00:26:42.406 --> 00:26:45.842
I don't know, but she looks good.


00:26:46.510 --> 00:26:50.844
I mean, not good like us. Good like bad.
Pff.


00:26:52.182 --> 00:26:54.946
DUSTIN: Here they come.
- All right, be cool. Be cool.


00:27:00.524 --> 00:27:02.253
JOEY:
Hi.


00:27:02.693 --> 00:27:06.527
You really know how to make an entrance.
That, uh, dress is amazing.


00:27:07.598 --> 00:27:10.533
Thank you. That's a nice cape.


00:27:12.136 --> 00:27:14.536
I mean, coat. It's a nice coat...


00:27:14.838 --> 00:27:17.033
- What should I do?
- Say something. Anything.


00:27:17.207 --> 00:27:18.936
- He's cute.
- Um...


00:27:19.109 --> 00:27:21.669
Hey, do you want some punch?


00:27:22.112 --> 00:27:23.875
Or you have some... Cool, okay.


00:27:30.788 --> 00:27:31.948
Weird.


00:27:32.122 --> 00:27:34.488
- Are you supposed to be Cupid?
- Yeah. Smart girl.


00:27:35.059 --> 00:27:36.117
Dope, right?


00:27:36.293 --> 00:27:39.558
With these arrows of love,
somebody gonna fall hard tonight.


00:27:39.730 --> 00:27:42.062
- Is that so?
- Yeah.


00:27:42.232 --> 00:27:44.427
Usually, I'm a lot cooler than this.


00:27:44.601 --> 00:27:47.399
I'm actually, like,
Joey Parker's best friend, see?


00:27:47.571 --> 00:27:50.699
- Is that supposed to impress me?
- Yeah, a little.


00:27:51.141 --> 00:27:53.166
You wanna see my Cupid dance?


00:28:03.554 --> 00:28:06.250
- What was that?
- I don't usually come to these things.


00:28:06.423 --> 00:28:07.720
Yeah, me too.


00:28:07.891 --> 00:28:10.257
What? Wait. Do you, um, wanna...?


00:28:10.427 --> 00:28:12.190
Wait. You don't like to dance?


00:28:12.363 --> 00:28:13.591
Sorry, what?


00:28:14.264 --> 00:28:16.095
- Do you wanna...?
- Hey.


00:28:16.266 --> 00:28:17.927
Can I ask you to dance?


00:28:19.470 --> 00:28:21.529
Yes, I'd love to.


00:28:26.443 --> 00:28:28.172
Now, don't take this the wrong way...


00:28:28.345 --> 00:28:31.075
...but I have never seen anything like you
in my life.


00:28:31.248 --> 00:28:33.148
- That's a good thing, right?
- Yes.


00:28:33.317 --> 00:28:34.841
Dance with me, Cupid-man.


00:28:39.356 --> 00:28:42.519
Do me a favor. Can you play this for me?
Track five.


00:28:42.693 --> 00:28:44.661
Here, hold this for me.


00:28:44.828 --> 00:28:45.817
Hey.


00:28:45.996 --> 00:28:47.020
[TANGO MUSIC PLAYING]


00:28:47.197 --> 00:28:49.256
GIRL:
Shake it, baby.


00:28:49.666 --> 00:28:50.690
Nice.


00:29:02.413 --> 00:29:05.541
- What was that?
- I guess the music just speaks to me.


00:29:11.789 --> 00:29:14.189
Well, I guess
we don't have a language barrier.


00:29:15.559 --> 00:29:18.960
Isn't that funny? I just love monkeys too.
Anyway, she'd...


00:29:20.864 --> 00:29:22.456
Look at him move.


00:29:22.633 --> 00:29:24.260
That has to be Joey.


00:29:24.435 --> 00:29:26.562
But who's the tramp?


00:29:49.159 --> 00:29:50.183
[CROWD CHEERING]


00:29:50.894 --> 00:29:51.918
Ow.


00:30:19.156 --> 00:30:20.384
[CHUCKLING]


00:30:31.368 --> 00:30:32.494
Oh...


00:30:32.669 --> 00:30:34.330
Oh, hey, are you okay?


00:30:37.407 --> 00:30:38.567
You were amazing.


00:30:38.742 --> 00:30:40.733
No, I wasn't. I fell.


00:30:44.381 --> 00:30:45.405
Joey?


00:30:47.084 --> 00:30:48.108
[CLOCK CHIMING]


00:30:50.921 --> 00:30:52.650
I have to go.


00:30:54.091 --> 00:30:55.991
I have to go. Can I have it back?


00:30:56.159 --> 00:30:58.525
- Today?
GIRL: Is that Joey?


00:30:58.695 --> 00:31:00.162
Wait, wait...


00:31:00.330 --> 00:31:01.820
- I'm late.
- Where are you...?


00:31:02.666 --> 00:31:04.065
JOEY:
Wait.


00:31:11.141 --> 00:31:12.733
MARY:
Oh, my God. That was...


00:31:12.910 --> 00:31:15.879
TAMI: Holy cow...
- I feel like I have to throw up.


00:31:16.046 --> 00:31:18.708
Tami, if I don't get home by midnight,
I am dead.


00:31:18.882 --> 00:31:20.941
You were dancing with Joey Parker.


00:31:21.118 --> 00:31:24.349
I fell on my butt with Joey Parker.
God, I knew I shouldn't have come.


00:31:24.521 --> 00:31:28.355
- He was into you.
- Because he didn't know who I was.


00:31:28.625 --> 00:31:30.115
You really think he was into me?


00:31:30.294 --> 00:31:31.955
[TRANSMISSION GRINDING]


00:31:35.732 --> 00:31:36.790
[ENGINE RATTLING]


00:31:39.469 --> 00:31:43.235
- I'm so sorry.
- No, no, no, this can't be happening.


00:31:50.814 --> 00:31:52.805
[SPEAKING IN CHINESE]


00:32:00.457 --> 00:32:01.788
[GASPS]


00:32:08.532 --> 00:32:12.491
I am not doing
that old diva's talk show again.


00:32:13.270 --> 00:32:14.669
She's got a serious... What?


00:32:15.739 --> 00:32:17.070
Oh, God.


00:32:17.240 --> 00:32:21.506
She's got a serious case
of the grab-hands.


00:32:23.213 --> 00:32:26.046
No, no, no, she's right behind me.
Go, go, go.


00:32:29.486 --> 00:32:31.147
No, no, no!


00:32:31.321 --> 00:32:34.256
That's my answer
to all those talk shows. No!


00:32:39.029 --> 00:32:41.623
Go that way, that way, that way. Go.


00:32:48.405 --> 00:32:51.203
Hmm. Well, it seems you managed
to follow orders.


00:32:51.742 --> 00:32:52.868
For once.


00:32:53.777 --> 00:32:55.802
Why are you wearing my robe?


00:32:56.179 --> 00:32:59.376
I was admiring its silky quality.


00:33:02.619 --> 00:33:07.147
You like my after-party?
It's a total rager, isn't it? Ha-ha.


00:33:07.591 --> 00:33:10.219
Oh, it's not a rager at all.


00:33:10.394 --> 00:33:12.487
No one's coming.


00:33:12.763 --> 00:33:16.722
I'm a Little Miss Not-So-Popular too.


00:33:17.734 --> 00:33:20.703
God, I'm so tired.


00:33:27.210 --> 00:33:29.007
[MOUTHS]
<i>Thank you.</i>


00:33:33.684 --> 00:33:38.314
All right, now, look. If you pull this off,
you will be the prince of all princes, okay?


00:33:38.488 --> 00:33:42.015
- Now, just let me talk to the teacher.
- Why aren't you two in class?


00:33:44.761 --> 00:33:47.161
I have a huge favor to ask, Miss B.


00:33:47.330 --> 00:33:49.890
I need to find somebody
who was at the dance last night.


00:33:50.067 --> 00:33:51.932
And if you don't, you'll die?


00:33:53.470 --> 00:33:55.097
I think I might.


00:33:56.873 --> 00:33:58.773
GIRL: No way.
BOY: Yeah.


00:33:58.942 --> 00:34:01.604
Whoever she was, she was a freak show.


00:34:01.778 --> 00:34:04.611
Totally.
Who runs away from Joey Parker?


00:34:04.781 --> 00:34:06.043
Not me.


00:34:06.216 --> 00:34:08.013
She'll never show her face now.


00:34:11.254 --> 00:34:13.017
We missed you at the ball, Mary.


00:34:13.190 --> 00:34:16.125
I guess a maid's job is just never done.


00:34:17.427 --> 00:34:19.292
[PA CHIMES]


00:34:19.763 --> 00:34:23.426
This is an administrative announcement
from the administrative office.


00:34:23.600 --> 00:34:25.090
[LAUGHING]


00:34:26.002 --> 00:34:27.196
What's up?


00:34:27.370 --> 00:34:29.565
You're on the mike
with the Funk master.


00:34:29.740 --> 00:34:31.173
[LAUGHING]


00:34:31.341 --> 00:34:35.141
- Okay, very funny. Keep the voices down.
- <i>Check it out. Listen up.</i>


00:34:35.312 --> 00:34:37.644
[RAPPING] <i>Once upon a time</i>
<i>There was this chill hottie</i>


00:34:37.814 --> 00:34:40.214
<i>She left Joey Parker</i>
<i>Now, that was real naughty</i>


00:34:40.383 --> 00:34:42.374
<i>Now here's JP just to tell you more</i>


00:34:42.552 --> 00:34:44.986
<i>Now, put down your pencils</i>
<i>And give JP the floor</i>


00:34:45.155 --> 00:34:46.816
All right, Funk, Funk, that's good.


00:34:46.990 --> 00:34:48.321
[DUSTIN]
<i>'Cause I was on the mike...</i>


00:34:48.492 --> 00:34:50.926
- All right, I got another verse.
- Funk, thank you.


00:34:51.094 --> 00:34:53.756
- You're welcome.
- That was the Funk, ladies and gentlemen.


00:34:53.930 --> 00:34:55.227
<i>Anyway...</i>


00:34:55.398 --> 00:34:58.492
...last night, I, uh...
I danced with somebody at the ball.


00:34:59.035 --> 00:35:01.333
<i>And you dropped your Zune</i>
<i>when you left.</i>


00:35:01.505 --> 00:35:04.804
<i>I'd love to return it.</i>
<i>The problem is, I don't know who you are.</i>


00:35:05.275 --> 00:35:06.936
And this is important...


00:35:07.110 --> 00:35:10.944
<i>... because you made</i>
<i>it one of the best nights of my life.</i>


00:35:11.248 --> 00:35:12.272
I...


00:35:12.449 --> 00:35:14.110
...love him.


00:35:14.284 --> 00:35:17.014
You have bacon in your braces.


00:35:17.187 --> 00:35:18.848
Keep the voices down.


00:35:20.257 --> 00:35:22.452
Okay, so here's the deal. Uh...


00:35:22.626 --> 00:35:25.220
If you were the girl
that I danced with last night...


00:35:25.395 --> 00:35:29.456
<i>... tell me the names of the four</i>
<i>most-listened-to songs on your playlist.</i>


00:35:29.633 --> 00:35:30.861
Thanks, mystery girl.


00:35:31.034 --> 00:35:32.262
<i>I'll be waiting.</i>


00:35:32.435 --> 00:35:35.165
"Thanks, mystery girl. I'll be waiting."


00:35:38.542 --> 00:35:41.067
- That was good. That was good.
- Was that all right?


00:35:41.244 --> 00:35:42.871
This is gonna be easy.


00:35:43.046 --> 00:35:44.536
[SOBBING]


00:35:44.714 --> 00:35:49.276
I know. I know, sweetie.
It's okay, but you gotta go, okay? All right.


00:35:49.452 --> 00:35:51.784
Just... All right, yeah. Whoo.


00:35:51.955 --> 00:35:54.287
Everybody, please,
single-file line, all right?


00:35:54.457 --> 00:35:56.448
You guys are so not his mystery girl.


00:35:56.626 --> 00:35:59.060
All right, everybody's gonna get a chance
to meet JP.


00:35:59.229 --> 00:36:00.457
You call me. Ha-ha.


00:36:00.630 --> 00:36:03.360
All right, all right. Cynthia? It's your turn.


00:36:03.533 --> 00:36:04.795
- You ready?
- Yes.


00:36:04.968 --> 00:36:06.458
All right, good.


00:36:06.636 --> 00:36:08.263
Look excited.


00:36:08.805 --> 00:36:09.829
Hey.


00:36:10.006 --> 00:36:15.740
"Push," "High," "Boys Don't Cry,"
and "Lullaby," all by the Cure.


00:36:17.747 --> 00:36:19.908
Now give me my Zune.


00:36:20.851 --> 00:36:22.250
I'm sorry, that's not it.


00:36:22.853 --> 00:36:25.253
- All right, I'm sorry. It's okay.
- Get off.


00:36:26.823 --> 00:36:27.847
[SIGHS]


00:36:28.024 --> 00:36:29.321
Hey.


00:36:29.593 --> 00:36:31.561
Mind if I pick up the slack
you don't want?


00:36:31.728 --> 00:36:33.821
- Knock yourself out.
- I will.


00:36:35.098 --> 00:36:36.531
God, they're all the same.


00:36:37.534 --> 00:36:39.024
But that girl from last night.


00:36:39.603 --> 00:36:42.197
- Special.
- Yeah, man, I saw it, man.


00:36:42.639 --> 00:36:47.804
I mean, I haven't seen you dance like that
since the 2006 VMAs, remember that night?


00:36:47.978 --> 00:36:49.275
It's pretty funky.


00:36:49.446 --> 00:36:51.607
So look, we're gonna find her, all right?


00:36:52.282 --> 00:36:53.874
She's here somewhere.


00:36:54.284 --> 00:36:56.616
I think she helped you
get your mojo back.


00:36:56.786 --> 00:36:59.186
Yeah, you're with me.


00:36:59.356 --> 00:37:00.948
- Let's do it.
- Who's next?


00:37:01.124 --> 00:37:03.649
Come on, ladies, have your songs ready.


00:37:03.827 --> 00:37:05.920
Oh, my gosh. He wasn't kidding.


00:37:06.096 --> 00:37:09.031
Go down and tell him it was you
before someone starts a riot.


00:37:09.199 --> 00:37:10.223
Forget it, Tami.


00:37:10.400 --> 00:37:13.563
He said last night
was one of the best nights of his life.


00:37:13.737 --> 00:37:16.604
- Yeah.
- Until he finds out it was me.


00:37:18.708 --> 00:37:21.575
- Are you listening? Come on.
- No. What?


00:37:24.748 --> 00:37:26.613
BRITT:
Stop right there.


00:37:27.884 --> 00:37:31.376
Oh, look at you, acting all innocent.


00:37:31.554 --> 00:37:34.853
- What are you talking about?
BREE: We know, Mary.


00:37:35.025 --> 00:37:38.324
- What?
- It was you at the ball. With Joey.


00:37:40.096 --> 00:37:42.064
- You guys are crazy.
- No, you're crazy...


00:37:42.232 --> 00:37:45.463
...if you think we'll let you end up
with Joey, Miss Stalker Face.


00:37:45.635 --> 00:37:48.069
And if you tell him it was you...


00:37:48.238 --> 00:37:50.206
...this video will be everywhere.


00:37:50.373 --> 00:37:51.840
Hello, YouTube.


00:37:52.008 --> 00:37:55.000
You barely know how to work the toaster,
let alone YouTube.


00:37:55.178 --> 00:37:57.078
Well, try us.


00:37:57.814 --> 00:37:59.839
Now, go make the lamb chops.


00:38:00.016 --> 00:38:01.779
Mother's very hungry.


00:38:06.423 --> 00:38:07.913
Where are you going?


00:38:08.091 --> 00:38:11.527
None of your beeswax. I mean, nowhere.


00:38:11.695 --> 00:38:14.687
For a walk. In the woods.


00:38:16.032 --> 00:38:17.556
Okay.


00:38:18.401 --> 00:38:19.766
Ow! Oh...


00:38:23.406 --> 00:38:26.773
If I were a playlist,
where would I hide myself?


00:38:35.485 --> 00:38:37.851
In plain sight.


00:38:38.021 --> 00:38:39.454
Brilliant.


00:38:41.825 --> 00:38:44.885
"We All Fall Down."
"She Wants to Move."


00:38:50.467 --> 00:38:51.491
[BRITT GROANS]


00:39:02.345 --> 00:39:07.009
Do you think maybe you could give me
a clue as to what the songs are?


00:39:07.617 --> 00:39:09.278
Are they emo?


00:39:09.452 --> 00:39:11.113
Techno?


00:39:11.554 --> 00:39:12.885
Young contemporary?


00:39:13.056 --> 00:39:17.493
Okay, people, people.
Please, disperse, okay?


00:39:17.660 --> 00:39:18.922
He's gonna take a break...


00:39:19.095 --> 00:39:23.156
...and you guys can just come line up
after class or something, all right?


00:39:23.333 --> 00:39:26.029
- I'm never gonna find her.
- Hey, hey, hey, mister.


00:39:26.202 --> 00:39:29.535
I don't wanna hear that crazy talk.
You leave that in crazy town, okay?


00:39:29.706 --> 00:39:33.039
Remember, you're Joey Parker,
and Joey Parker always gets his girl.


00:39:33.209 --> 00:39:34.608
I'm right. You know I'm right.


00:39:35.011 --> 00:39:37.912
All right, what's your name? Say it, huh?


00:39:38.081 --> 00:39:40.242
- I'm...
- Joey Parker.


00:39:40.417 --> 00:39:42.783
Your prayers have been answered.


00:39:42.952 --> 00:39:44.351
Whoa, whoa, whoa.


00:39:45.221 --> 00:39:48.418
Look, Britt, okay?
Joey is on break, okay?


00:39:48.591 --> 00:39:49.990
And he's exhausted...


00:39:50.160 --> 00:39:52.424
Oh, I'm not here to talk to Joey.


00:39:52.595 --> 00:39:54.062
I'm in the mood for some funk.


00:39:56.166 --> 00:39:58.794
- Really?
- No. Now, get out of my way.


00:40:01.337 --> 00:40:04.397
I'm the one.


00:40:05.108 --> 00:40:06.132
[SCOFFS]


00:40:06.943 --> 00:40:09.070
You're kidding me, right?


00:40:09.245 --> 00:40:12.476
I can totally prove it.
I know all the songs on the Zune.


00:40:13.450 --> 00:40:14.883
Prove it.


00:40:15.618 --> 00:40:19.486
"We All Fall Down," "She Wants to Move,"
"Pon de Replay," and "Hips Don't Lie."


00:40:21.524 --> 00:40:22.821
I'm right, right?


00:40:23.526 --> 00:40:25.494
I knew it!


00:40:25.829 --> 00:40:28.195
Well, what are you waiting for?


00:40:28.565 --> 00:40:31.056
- Kiss me.
- No, no, no.


00:40:31.234 --> 00:40:32.496
We're gonna dance first.


00:40:32.669 --> 00:40:34.432
What?


00:40:35.338 --> 00:40:38.068
But you said we only needed
to know the songs.


00:40:38.241 --> 00:40:40.869
Plus, I'm not warmed up.
And there's no music.


00:40:41.044 --> 00:40:44.172
Well, if you were the one,
you wouldn't need music.


00:40:44.347 --> 00:40:46.247
- Sorry, Britt.
- Wait.


00:40:47.484 --> 00:40:49.247
I don't need music.


00:40:50.520 --> 00:40:52.852
I love to dance and sing.


00:40:53.022 --> 00:40:54.512
BOY:
Are you kidding me?


00:40:54.991 --> 00:40:59.860
[SINGING] <i>Oh, babe, you want it like that</i>
<i>You want it like this</i>


00:41:00.763 --> 00:41:03.197
I just lose control when I'm dancing.


00:41:03.800 --> 00:41:05.631
I love it so much.


00:41:05.802 --> 00:41:07.269
<i>Oh, baby</i>


00:41:08.004 --> 00:41:09.699
Come on.


00:41:09.873 --> 00:41:11.738
What is with her?


00:41:11.908 --> 00:41:14.376
<i>Like that</i>
<i>You like it like that</i>


00:41:15.879 --> 00:41:19.406
How dare they hold that tape against you?
You were 11.


00:41:19.582 --> 00:41:23.985
What do I do? I don't want Joey to think
I'm Little Miss Stalker.


00:41:24.521 --> 00:41:26.648
You and Joey connected out there.


00:41:26.823 --> 00:41:30.122
Even if he sees the tape,
he's not gonna think you're a crazy stalker.


00:41:30.293 --> 00:41:32.022
I hope.


00:41:33.029 --> 00:41:35.224
I feel nauseous.


00:41:35.398 --> 00:41:37.457
- All right, dude?
- Yeah, fine.


00:41:43.106 --> 00:41:44.198
Whoa. Um...


00:41:44.374 --> 00:41:47.707
- Awkward.
- Ready to meet your mystery girl?


00:41:48.311 --> 00:41:50.506
Of course, you know the songs too.


00:41:50.680 --> 00:41:51.704
God, no.


00:41:51.881 --> 00:41:54.076
But I'm the real freaking one.


00:41:54.250 --> 00:41:57.549
And I freaking love you
and you just better freaking love me back...


00:41:57.720 --> 00:42:00.450
...because I'm the freaking one,
you freak.


00:42:01.157 --> 00:42:05.150
Way, way, way deep inside...


00:42:05.328 --> 00:42:07.262
...I'm sure you're a lovely person.


00:42:08.097 --> 00:42:10.088
I can prove I'm the one.


00:42:11.868 --> 00:42:13.859
Through dance.


00:42:22.212 --> 00:42:23.338
What?


00:42:23.513 --> 00:42:28.075
Okay, if this shows up on TMZ,
my attorneys will eat you all for lunch.


00:42:28.251 --> 00:42:29.548
Literally.


00:42:29.719 --> 00:42:31.550
You should talk to him.


00:42:31.721 --> 00:42:34.713
Love can bring any man... Oh, look!


00:42:34.891 --> 00:42:37.416
I'll check a couple parties.
I'll call if I get a lead.


00:42:37.594 --> 00:42:39.858
It's show time. You can do this.


00:42:41.231 --> 00:42:42.255
- I can do it.
- Yeah.


00:42:42.432 --> 00:42:43.865
Okay.


00:42:44.033 --> 00:42:47.298
- Wait, let's go get some food.
- No.


00:42:47.470 --> 00:42:49.631
I'm done with this.
There's no... Ridiculous.


00:42:49.806 --> 00:42:51.205
- Joey?
- Yeah.


00:42:51.641 --> 00:42:53.506
I have something important to tell you.


00:42:53.676 --> 00:42:56.543
- Oh, hey. You work for Dominique, right?
- What?


00:42:56.713 --> 00:42:59.045
No, no, that's...


00:43:00.083 --> 00:43:02.051
You had shrimp in your hair.


00:43:02.852 --> 00:43:06.879
Well, no. No, I mean, yes, that was me,
but that's not what I wanted to tell you.


00:43:07.056 --> 00:43:09.547
- Um, I'm...
- Dominique is relentless.


00:43:10.526 --> 00:43:12.926
Bree, Britt and now her.


00:43:13.896 --> 00:43:17.923
Look, I'm looking for somebody
and I don't have the time right now to talk.


00:43:18.101 --> 00:43:19.363
I gotta go, I'm sorry.


00:43:20.403 --> 00:43:22.268
But it was nice seeing you.


00:43:35.051 --> 00:43:36.518
Yes. Hello? Okay.


00:43:36.686 --> 00:43:39.587
Could you please connect me
to the YouTube?


00:43:41.224 --> 00:43:42.953
No, you don't understand. I have...


00:43:43.126 --> 00:43:46.061
- I told you.
- Oh, my God. He blew you off?


00:43:46.696 --> 00:43:49.756
People like me don't belong
with people like him anyway. Whatever.


00:43:51.301 --> 00:43:52.859
Damn.


00:43:55.938 --> 00:43:56.927
[INTERCOM BEEPS]


00:43:57.106 --> 00:44:00.041
DOMINIQUE: <i>Mary, I need you to</i>
<i>finalize the menu for the girls' party.</i>


00:44:00.209 --> 00:44:03.110
<i>And have Dr. Woo move up</i>
<i>my high colonic to this afternoon.</i>


00:44:03.279 --> 00:44:04.769
<i>I'm feeling blocked.</i>


00:44:04.947 --> 00:44:07.313
<i>Have your sisters' moved up too.</i>


00:44:08.584 --> 00:44:11.280
What else do I have to live for?


00:44:11.788 --> 00:44:14.518
<i>That's the spirit, sweetie.</i>


00:44:15.625 --> 00:44:17.616
[MUSIC PLAYING]


00:44:20.663 --> 00:44:22.460
[SINGING]
<i>Hold on</i>


00:44:22.632 --> 00:44:24.623
<i>Then I hear your phone a-ringing</i>


00:44:24.801 --> 00:44:28.237
<i>Just waiting for your voice to come on</i>


00:44:28.404 --> 00:44:29.769
Come on.


00:44:29.939 --> 00:44:32.066
Come on, pay attention to me.
Look at me.


00:44:32.241 --> 00:44:33.640
This is a treat for you.


00:44:33.810 --> 00:44:36.973
Oh, here. Crab cakes? Anyone?


00:44:38.781 --> 00:44:40.942
Hey. What are you doing here?


00:44:41.484 --> 00:44:42.849
Oh, I'm here to help.


00:44:43.019 --> 00:44:45.078
- I love you.
- I know.


00:44:45.254 --> 00:44:48.746
- Here. Start serving there. I'll get the rest.
- Okay.


00:44:50.426 --> 00:44:52.690
Hey, bro. Hey, bro.


00:44:52.862 --> 00:44:54.454
You want a crab cake?


00:44:55.865 --> 00:44:57.799
Yeah, man, the whole school is here.


00:44:57.967 --> 00:45:01.630
Just give me 20 minutes,
I'm gonna find your girl, all right?


00:45:02.171 --> 00:45:04.036
Gotta call you back.


00:45:04.407 --> 00:45:07.376
Hey, it's a party. Get off the phone.


00:45:09.612 --> 00:45:12.547
- Nice dance moves.
- Oh. Ha-ha-ha.


00:45:13.316 --> 00:45:16.911
You know, those purple highlights
look very familiar.


00:45:17.086 --> 00:45:21.489
You might not recognize me
without my angel wings of love.


00:45:22.125 --> 00:45:23.524
- I'm the Funk.
- The what?


00:45:23.693 --> 00:45:25.217
You know, Cupid dance.


00:45:25.395 --> 00:45:27.454
You can't forget the Cupid dance.


00:45:27.630 --> 00:45:30.224
- Oh, sorry, no. No.
- No?


00:45:30.400 --> 00:45:32.368
I'm Joey Parker's best friend.


00:45:32.535 --> 00:45:34.469
Oh. Is that supposed to impress me?


00:45:34.637 --> 00:45:37.800
Ah, you are my mystery girl. I knew it.


00:45:37.974 --> 00:45:39.202
Hey, is your friend here?


00:45:39.375 --> 00:45:41.400
What, Mary? Yeah, she's here.


00:45:41.577 --> 00:45:44.671
Can you go get her? I'm gonna call Joey.
We have to hook them up.


00:45:44.847 --> 00:45:45.871
He is in love.


00:45:46.048 --> 00:45:48.175
- Seriously? Seriously?
- Yeah. Yeah.


00:45:48.351 --> 00:45:51.514
- Awesome, I'll be right back. Okay.
- Okay.


00:45:53.156 --> 00:45:55.147
[PHONE RINGS]


00:45:56.125 --> 00:45:57.786
Dustin.


00:45:57.960 --> 00:46:00.258
- What up?
- Why does it sound like you're frowning?


00:46:00.430 --> 00:46:02.625
You better not be frowning.
What did I tell you?


00:46:02.799 --> 00:46:04.562
- What's your name?
- We're not playing...


00:46:04.734 --> 00:46:06.827
<i>We do it until you cheer up.</i>
<i>What's your name?</i>


00:46:07.003 --> 00:46:09.267
- Joey Parker.
- Who keeps it funky?


00:46:09.439 --> 00:46:11.430
- Joey Parker.
- Right. And who keeps it real?


00:46:11.607 --> 00:46:14.075
- <i>Joey Parker.</i>
- Joey Parker keeps it real, am I right?


00:46:14.243 --> 00:46:15.642
You're stupid is what you are.


00:46:15.812 --> 00:46:18.940
- Joey Parker, let me hear you screaming.
- I'm in front of her house.


00:46:19.115 --> 00:46:20.673
I know, but scream it out loud.


00:46:20.850 --> 00:46:23.216
- Joey Parker!
- <i>Joey Parker, that's right. Look.</i>


00:46:23.386 --> 00:46:26.753
All evidence indicates that your girl
is in the spot.


00:46:26.923 --> 00:46:29.221
- For real?
- <i>Your girl's inside. Come on.</i>


00:46:29.392 --> 00:46:30.882
Copy that.


00:46:32.028 --> 00:46:34.189
DOMINIQUE:
There's my girls, see?


00:46:34.764 --> 00:46:36.698
- Yeah.
- Ow!


00:46:36.866 --> 00:46:39.300
Chins up. Chins up. Tummies in.


00:46:39.469 --> 00:46:41.130
Yes.


00:46:43.473 --> 00:46:45.873
- Oh. Happy birthday.
- Thanks.


00:46:51.647 --> 00:46:54.946
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Stop right there,
Mr. Man.


00:46:55.485 --> 00:46:58.477
I'm the one, Joey Parker.


00:46:58.654 --> 00:46:59.712
So let's duet.


00:47:00.223 --> 00:47:01.588
You know, duet?


00:47:01.757 --> 00:47:03.588
You get it? Duet.


00:47:03.759 --> 00:47:05.317
Do a duet with me.


00:47:05.495 --> 00:47:08.293
Um, not if the human race
depended on it.


00:47:08.731 --> 00:47:09.823
Well, that's rude.


00:47:09.999 --> 00:47:13.230
Now, I wouldn't do a duet
with you, mister...


00:47:13.402 --> 00:47:16.030
...if we were the last two people
alive, okay?


00:47:16.205 --> 00:47:18.400
And the world was taken over by apes...


00:47:18.574 --> 00:47:21.065
...and we were the only two
with opposable thumbs...


00:47:21.244 --> 00:47:23.178
...I still wouldn't.


00:47:26.215 --> 00:47:27.239
Crab cakes?


00:47:27.416 --> 00:47:28.713
- It's fate.
- What?


00:47:28.885 --> 00:47:31.012
He's here. Now's your chance.


00:47:31.187 --> 00:47:34.156
I don't know what she's wearing.
I just know that she's here.


00:47:34.323 --> 00:47:35.950
I'm a little nervous, man.


00:47:36.125 --> 00:47:37.456
Go and talk to him.


00:47:37.627 --> 00:47:39.857
- Fine, okay, I'll go.
- Go, go, go.


00:47:40.029 --> 00:47:41.326
I hope we find her.


00:47:43.499 --> 00:47:44.523
Oh, hey.


00:47:45.268 --> 00:47:49.034
- Um... Crab cake?
- Thanks.


00:47:49.205 --> 00:47:52.766
- Can I ask you a question?
- Sure.


00:47:52.942 --> 00:47:57.174
Have you seen a girl here that can dance
like you've never seen a girl dance before?


00:47:57.346 --> 00:47:59.940
Actually, Joey, yes.


00:48:02.585 --> 00:48:05.782
- It's funny because you're looking...
MARY [ON TAPE]: <i>I love you so much, Joey.</i>


00:48:05.955 --> 00:48:07.684
<i>And you are totally kissable.</i>


00:48:07.857 --> 00:48:09.722
[CROWD LAUGHING]


00:48:09.892 --> 00:48:11.723
<i>This is for you.</i>


00:48:18.301 --> 00:48:19.325
[IMITATES CHICKEN]


00:48:19.502 --> 00:48:20.901
This can't be happening.


00:48:21.737 --> 00:48:24.570
Is that you?


00:48:25.541 --> 00:48:27.941
No, it's okay.


00:48:32.882 --> 00:48:34.873
[SOBBING]


00:48:58.774 --> 00:49:00.765
[TANGO MUSIC PLAYING]


00:49:11.020 --> 00:49:13.352
- You guys hear that?
- Yeah.


00:49:22.565 --> 00:49:23.589
Uh...


00:49:23.766 --> 00:49:25.631
I'll be right back.


00:49:25.801 --> 00:49:27.291
[GIGGLING]


00:49:37.113 --> 00:49:38.910
You're the one.


00:49:47.390 --> 00:49:49.415
I think this is yours.


00:49:53.362 --> 00:49:55.523
You tried to tell me at school too...


00:49:55.698 --> 00:49:57.791
...and I was a jerk to you.


00:49:59.101 --> 00:50:01.626
Wow, you're the one.


00:50:01.804 --> 00:50:04.671
I actually found you. This is amazing.


00:50:05.775 --> 00:50:07.208
It's cold, huh?


00:50:07.376 --> 00:50:08.400
Hey, um...


00:50:09.979 --> 00:50:12.447
- No.
- Take my jacket. No, really.


00:50:17.086 --> 00:50:19.418
You don't have to pretend
like you like me.


00:50:19.588 --> 00:50:21.647
I've had enough charity to last a lifetime.


00:50:22.291 --> 00:50:24.919
Who said anything about charity?


00:50:25.194 --> 00:50:27.822
I've been going crazy looking for you.


00:50:27.997 --> 00:50:29.624
I couldn't stop thinking about you.


00:50:30.099 --> 00:50:31.691
The way that we moved together.


00:50:33.069 --> 00:50:36.470
Well, my mom was a dancer.
So I guess it's in my blood.


00:50:40.976 --> 00:50:44.309
So you really think I'm totally kissable?


00:50:44.814 --> 00:50:46.338
What? No, that was...


00:50:47.116 --> 00:50:51.678
That was... I was a kid. I didn't... Pff. No.
Ha-ha.


00:50:52.121 --> 00:50:54.055
That's too bad. I thought it was cool.


00:50:56.459 --> 00:50:57.892
Wow, I...


00:50:58.260 --> 00:50:59.887
I know I barely know you...


00:51:00.062 --> 00:51:01.552
...but...


00:51:02.698 --> 00:51:05.189
Can I...? I wanna take you out, Mary.


00:51:06.969 --> 00:51:11.065
DOMINIQUE: Mary, get in here.
- And that's my cue.


00:51:13.209 --> 00:51:15.507
Wait, you gonna give me an answer?


00:51:16.345 --> 00:51:17.835
Yes.


00:51:22.585 --> 00:51:24.485
[ALARM BEEPING]


00:51:39.935 --> 00:51:41.425
[MARY SCREAMS]


00:51:50.312 --> 00:51:51.506
Joey.


00:51:51.680 --> 00:51:54.308
Whoa. Hey, Tony Hawk, slow down.
You know you're in a hallway.


00:51:54.483 --> 00:51:57.350
Guess who has an audition for
the Academy of Performing Arts.


00:51:57.520 --> 00:51:58.612
Me, that's who.


00:51:58.788 --> 00:52:01.552
They narrowed the applicants,
500 to 20. I'm in the top 20.


00:52:01.724 --> 00:52:04.192
Someone's gonna call, let me know
when my audition is.


00:52:04.360 --> 00:52:06.692
I'm so close I can feel it.
My gosh, Mary, breathe.


00:52:06.862 --> 00:52:09.956
- Breathe. Breathe.
- Mary, that's amazing. That's amazing.


00:52:10.132 --> 00:52:13.226
Wow. Hey, you want me to show you
some moves? Uh...


00:52:13.402 --> 00:52:15.768
For your audition.
I can help you practice.


00:52:15.938 --> 00:52:18.099
I might be into that.


00:52:18.407 --> 00:52:19.669
You might be into that?


00:52:19.842 --> 00:52:21.275
[BELL RINGS]


00:52:21.443 --> 00:52:23.104
Meet me tomorrow.


00:52:23.746 --> 00:52:25.236
[PHONE RINGING]


00:52:28.684 --> 00:52:29.708
Speak.


00:52:29.885 --> 00:52:33.821
Hello. I'm calling from the Manhattan
Academy of Performing Arts...


00:52:33.989 --> 00:52:37.390
...regarding an application
for Mary Santiago.


00:52:37.560 --> 00:52:39.585
I'm her guardian. Talk faster.


00:52:40.896 --> 00:52:42.625
We'd like to schedule an audition.


00:52:42.798 --> 00:52:45.892
Oh, no, no, no. That won't do.


00:52:46.802 --> 00:52:49.202
She can't dance.


00:52:49.371 --> 00:52:50.736
She broke both her legs.


00:52:53.175 --> 00:52:55.075
Oh, my goodness. That's awful. How?


00:52:55.244 --> 00:52:59.180
Well, they're chicken legs
and they were very weak...


00:52:59.348 --> 00:53:01.009
...and they just snapped.


00:53:01.450 --> 00:53:02.917
<i>Like twigs.</i>


00:53:03.085 --> 00:53:05.280
We'd appreciate it
if you didn't call again...


00:53:05.454 --> 00:53:11.256
...because, well, it just reminds us
that her dance career is over.


00:53:12.494 --> 00:53:14.758
Hey, I'm going clubbing in Vegas
this weekend...


00:53:14.930 --> 00:53:17.763
...you wouldn't happen to know
what the weather is like?


00:53:17.933 --> 00:53:19.264
[PHONE CLICKS]


00:53:19.435 --> 00:53:20.629
Hello?


00:53:21.370 --> 00:53:23.167
DOMINIQUE:
Hurry up and drive. I'm late.


00:53:23.339 --> 00:53:26.900
If I miss this flight, it's your fault,
you nimrod.


00:53:28.277 --> 00:53:30.905
Well, there goes the wicked witch
of the west.


00:53:31.080 --> 00:53:32.479
Maybe she took her broomstick.


00:53:32.648 --> 00:53:35.344
- You're off the hook for the weekend.
- Ha-ha-ha. Yeah.


00:53:38.721 --> 00:53:40.154
You have to be kidding me.


00:53:40.322 --> 00:53:42.381
- She's driving me nuts.
- What is it?


00:53:45.794 --> 00:53:47.625
Okay, wow. Um...


00:53:47.796 --> 00:53:49.855
"Paint the pool pink.


00:53:50.032 --> 00:53:52.227
Regrout the tile.


00:53:52.401 --> 00:53:55.928
- Vacuum the driveway"? This is ridiculous.
- Chores from Dominique.


00:53:56.105 --> 00:53:59.563
She's gone and I have to do them
or who knows how long she'll ground me.


00:53:59.742 --> 00:54:01.141
Sorry, maybe another time.


00:54:01.310 --> 00:54:03.778
Unless you do your work
while you do her work.


00:54:09.451 --> 00:54:11.112
[SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]


00:55:06.175 --> 00:55:08.040
You're good. You are good, but I...


00:55:08.210 --> 00:55:10.770
I think we need to work on your
technique a little bit.


00:55:10.946 --> 00:55:11.970
Okay.


00:55:14.049 --> 00:55:17.314
Just, you need to loosen up
a little bit more.


00:55:18.721 --> 00:55:19.745
Not like that. No.


00:55:37.139 --> 00:55:38.163
- isn't so bad.


00:55:38.340 --> 00:55:41.332
He's doing all of her work.


00:55:41.677 --> 00:55:43.838
I feel very upset right now.


00:55:44.146 --> 00:55:45.841
Let's make her repaint the pool?


00:55:46.015 --> 00:55:51.078
Let's make her vacuum the driveway?
You're an idiot.


00:55:52.054 --> 00:55:53.783
MARY:
No. What are you doing? No.


00:55:53.956 --> 00:55:55.981
What's he see in that little freak show?


00:55:56.158 --> 00:55:58.956
Well, I think she's, like,
a good height for him.


00:55:59.128 --> 00:56:00.857
- And she has pretty hair...
- Shut up.


00:56:03.298 --> 00:56:05.129
We need a plan B.


00:56:09.104 --> 00:56:10.594
[STRING TWANGS]


00:56:11.840 --> 00:56:14.934
- Uh... I think you need a new guitar.
- Ha.


00:56:15.110 --> 00:56:17.101
Yeah, that'd be nice.


00:56:19.248 --> 00:56:21.182
You writing a new song?


00:56:22.084 --> 00:56:23.108
Yeah.


00:56:23.619 --> 00:56:25.849
You, uh, wanna help me
with the harmony?


00:56:26.889 --> 00:56:29.357
- No, I...
- I think you wanna help me with harmony.


00:56:29.525 --> 00:56:31.390
- Come on.
- Okay.


00:56:31.560 --> 00:56:33.118
Here.


00:56:34.630 --> 00:56:36.894
And this, this is as far as I got
with the lyrics.


00:56:37.066 --> 00:56:39.899
- Okay.
- Just start right here.


00:56:40.069 --> 00:56:41.400
- You ready?
- Yeah.


00:56:41.570 --> 00:56:43.197
Okay.


00:56:45.107 --> 00:56:47.701
[SINGING]
<i>It's become so hard</i>


00:56:47.876 --> 00:56:49.639
- <i>For me to be surprised</i>
- <i>For me to be surprised</i>


00:56:49.812 --> 00:56:50.836
That's good.


00:56:51.013 --> 00:56:53.777
- <i>But you're bringing back the real me</i>
- <i>But you're bringing back the real me</i>


00:56:53.949 --> 00:56:56.417
- <i>No judgment in your eyes</i>
- <i>No judgment in your eyes</i>


00:56:56.585 --> 00:56:59.452
- <i>It's the way you make me feel</i>
- <i>It's the way you make me feel</i>


00:56:59.621 --> 00:57:04.422
- <i>Like I'm finally something real</i>
- <i>Like I'm finally something real</i>


00:57:08.230 --> 00:57:09.390
Okay.


00:57:09.865 --> 00:57:11.628
Break time's over.


00:57:12.668 --> 00:57:15.136
Back to resting.


00:57:21.610 --> 00:57:23.373
[SIGHS]


00:57:23.545 --> 00:57:27.037
You know, one of the reasons I came back
was because I wanted to remember...


00:57:27.216 --> 00:57:30.151
...why I started dancing in the first place.


00:57:32.988 --> 00:57:35.013
Dancing with you...


00:57:35.757 --> 00:57:37.782
...I'm starting to remember.


00:57:40.028 --> 00:57:42.019
- Yeah?
- Yeah.


00:57:45.567 --> 00:57:47.091
And you're getting closer.


00:57:47.269 --> 00:57:48.463
So are you.


00:57:48.637 --> 00:57:52.198
- I mean with your moves.
- Well, you're not looking so bad yourself.


00:57:52.374 --> 00:57:54.569
Why don't we pick up again tomorrow,
right here?


00:57:54.743 --> 00:57:56.973
As in my house, as in this position?


00:57:57.146 --> 00:57:58.340
I'm not that kind of guy.


00:57:58.514 --> 00:58:01.483
Somehow I don't find that
entirely convincing.


00:58:08.891 --> 00:58:11.189
So where's Prince Charming now?


00:58:11.360 --> 00:58:14.329
Couldn't stand to spend another second
with his charity case?


00:58:14.496 --> 00:58:16.396
Wow, jealous much?


00:58:16.565 --> 00:58:17.759
[DOORBELL RINGS]


00:58:17.933 --> 00:58:21.664
Was that the doorbell? That's strange.
I wonder who that could be.


00:58:21.837 --> 00:58:24.499
I don't know, Bree.
Get that, would you, Mary?


00:58:24.673 --> 00:58:26.140
God, you guys are weird.


00:58:29.077 --> 00:58:31.443
Hello, plan B.


00:58:31.613 --> 00:58:33.342
Could you be more obvious?


00:58:33.515 --> 00:58:36.143
Well, no. That would totally give it away.


00:58:52.768 --> 00:58:54.292
Tami, what if he fell asleep?


00:58:54.469 --> 00:58:57.165
No way. Go. And call me later.


00:58:57.339 --> 00:58:59.705
Domifreak took my cell phone,
remember?


00:58:59.875 --> 00:59:01.672
Do you want me to wait?


00:59:01.977 --> 00:59:04.810
No, I'm good. Joey will take me home.
Thank you.


00:59:04.980 --> 00:59:06.971
- Go kill it.
- Okay.


00:59:21.630 --> 00:59:23.393
[SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]


00:59:31.907 --> 00:59:33.397
[GATE CLANGS]


00:59:37.713 --> 00:59:39.305
What was that?


00:59:39.748 --> 00:59:41.511
- What's going on?
- Nothing.


00:59:41.683 --> 00:59:44.413
Natalia. Natalia, look. Ha.


00:59:44.586 --> 00:59:46.986
We had a thing, but it's over.


00:59:47.923 --> 00:59:50.915
- Joey. Joey, come on.
- It's time for you to go.


00:59:51.093 --> 00:59:52.822
I'll see you at school.


01:00:24.726 --> 01:00:26.717
[SNORING]


01:00:26.895 --> 01:00:29.455
Hey, where have you been all night?


01:00:29.631 --> 01:00:32.532
I'm just doing a little yoga.


01:00:34.536 --> 01:00:38.404
Hey, have you been crying?
Or are you just naturally puffy?


01:00:38.573 --> 01:00:41.041
I never noticed that before.
What's wrong?


01:00:41.209 --> 01:00:44.042
- Dominique, I'd rather not talk about it.
- Oh, come on.


01:00:44.212 --> 01:00:46.146
Talk to me. Come on, sit down.


01:00:46.815 --> 01:00:49.477
Come on, sit down. Come on.


01:00:50.185 --> 01:00:51.652
Okay. Sit in the hand.


01:00:52.688 --> 01:00:54.747
Is it Joey, honey?


01:00:54.923 --> 01:00:57.551
Oh, I knew it.


01:00:57.726 --> 01:01:01.059
Did he find someone prettier
and more successful?


01:01:01.229 --> 01:01:04.392
Oh, I'm sorry. That is difficult.


01:01:04.566 --> 01:01:08.093
Not that I would know, but I did take
an acting class once. I can imagine.


01:01:08.970 --> 01:01:13.134
Let me give you a word of advice.
Joey is an <i>E! Hollywood True Story...</i>


01:01:13.308 --> 01:01:15.674
...just waiting to happen.


01:01:15.844 --> 01:01:18.438
There's no sense crying over him.
Mm-mm.


01:01:18.613 --> 01:01:21.104
In fact, it's kind of pathetic.


01:01:22.050 --> 01:01:24.518
I can't wait to get out of here
and move to Manhattan.


01:01:24.686 --> 01:01:28.087
Oh, I'm sorry. Did I forget to tell you?
I did, my bad.


01:01:28.256 --> 01:01:31.248
They called. There's no audition.
It was a mistake.


01:01:31.426 --> 01:01:34.259
- What? You're lying.
- No, I'm not.


01:01:34.429 --> 01:01:36.829
The rejection letter is right there
in that mess...


01:01:36.998 --> 01:01:40.365
...you need to clean up here
and sort through.


01:01:43.739 --> 01:01:45.639
I'm so glad we had this little talk.


01:01:45.807 --> 01:01:50.244
I've always wanted to be the mother
you'll never have.


01:01:53.548 --> 01:01:57.609
Yeah. So the Japan tour was awesome.
Like a Bruce Lee movie, but no subtitles.


01:01:57.786 --> 01:02:00.653
- The sushi kind of made me sick...
- Mary.


01:02:01.656 --> 01:02:04.056
Hey. Catch you in a minute.


01:02:04.226 --> 01:02:05.750
Mary.


01:02:06.428 --> 01:02:09.397
Mary, slow down. Hey, what...?


01:02:09.564 --> 01:02:10.724
What's wrong?


01:02:10.899 --> 01:02:13.424
I've been calling Tami,
trying to get ahold of you.


01:02:15.504 --> 01:02:18.166
- What did I do?
- It doesn't matter. It's done. We're done.


01:02:19.408 --> 01:02:20.807
Wait.


01:02:21.176 --> 01:02:22.666
Whoa, whoa.


01:02:22.844 --> 01:02:25.404
- What are you talking about?
- Did you feel sorry for me?


01:02:25.580 --> 01:02:28.048
Was I your charity case?
Is that why you asked me out?


01:02:28.216 --> 01:02:30.878
- What does that mean?
- You figured you'd toy with me...


01:02:31.052 --> 01:02:33.680
...until someone better came along
and I wouldn't mind...


01:02:33.855 --> 01:02:35.846
...because I was lucky
a big star wanted me.


01:02:36.124 --> 01:02:40.458
You know what really sucks about falling
for a guy you know you're not right for?


01:02:41.029 --> 01:02:44.624
You fall anyway because you think
he might turn out to be different.


01:02:45.333 --> 01:02:46.766
Mary.


01:02:48.737 --> 01:02:50.170
- I am different.
- Anyway...


01:02:50.338 --> 01:02:53.000
...thanks for all the dance moves,
but I'm done dancing.


01:02:53.175 --> 01:02:54.665
Goodbye.


01:02:57.078 --> 01:02:59.342
DUSTIN:
All right, time for some damage control.


01:02:59.514 --> 01:03:02.574
And what'd I tell you? My mystery girl.


01:03:07.322 --> 01:03:09.119
- Whoa, Tami.
- I need your help.


01:03:09.291 --> 01:03:11.259
- What's with the blinds?
- It's about Mary.


01:03:11.426 --> 01:03:14.122
- Come on, girl.
- Don't you "girl" me.


01:03:14.896 --> 01:03:17.091
Just give me a second.


01:03:17.265 --> 01:03:18.289
One second.


01:03:18.467 --> 01:03:21.630
Don't you have a stadium show to play
or something?


01:03:21.803 --> 01:03:23.065
Come on. Back door.


01:03:24.873 --> 01:03:26.238
